  "content": {
    "display_title": "Faithfulness of the representation on the CAR trace Hilbert space",
    "one_sentence_role": "Unitary conjugation preserves injectivity of the target-state representation.",
    "natural_language_statement": "Let $A$ be the completed CAR algebra and $\\tau$ its normalized trace. Fix a representative shell family and its chosen unitary links $L_j$ in the selected atomic representation $\\pi$. Write $T=C^*(\\pi(A),\\{L_j\\})$ for the resulting concrete target and $\\iota:A\\to T$, $\\iota(a)=\\pi(a)$, for its faithful unital source map. This fixes one target and one source map throughout. Let $(H_\\phi,\\rho_\\phi,\\xi_\\phi)$ be the GNS representation of the chosen state extension $\\phi$, and let $(H_\\tau,\\pi_\\tau,\\xi_\\tau)$ be the CAR trace GNS representation. Choose once the pointed unitary $E:H_\\tau\\to H_\\phi$ with $E\\xi_\\tau=\\xi_\\phi$ and $E\\pi_\\tau(a)=\\rho_\\phi(\\iota(a))E$. Then $\\widetilde\\rho(t)=E^{-1}\\rho_\\phi(t)E$ is injective on $T$.",
    "definition_explanation": null,
    "assumptions": "The family, extension, and chosen unitary are the ones used to define `traceModelRepresentation`. Faithfulness of $\\rho_\\phi$ is the separately proved kernel-dichotomy result.",
    "conclusion": "The same concrete target admits a faithful representation on the nonzero separable space $H_\\tau=L^2(A,\\tau)$. Its restriction to $A$ is the CAR trace representation.",
    "proof_summary": "Undo the same conjugation and apply faithfulness of the original target-state representation.",
    "proof_steps": [
      {
        "step_id": "s1",
        "text": "Suppose $\\widetilde\\rho(t)=\\widetilde\\rho(s)$. Since $E$ is a unitary onto $H_\\phi$,\n\n$$\\rho_\\phi(t)=E\\widetilde\\rho(t)E^{-1}=E\\widetilde\\rho(s)E^{-1}=\\rho_\\phi(s).$$\n\nThe theorem `tracialRepresentation_injective` then gives $t=s$. In the source this is the composition of the injective conjugation equivalence with the injective representation; it does not require another ideal argument."
      }
    ],
    "lean_realization_notes": "Injectivity concerns the homomorphism into operators, not a vector functional. The result does not assert irreducibility of this representation or norm separability of $T$. Conjugation uses the inverse on the left because $E$ points from the CAR space to the target-state space.",
    "content_completeness": "CARD_CONTENT_COMPLETE",
    "language_tag": "en"
  },
